  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: LCR40.44 reference to LCR40.87",
      "summary": "LCR40.44 sends segregated prime-brokerage balances to LCR40.87 (wholesale loan payments, 50% or 100%), while the rule for such balances sits in LCR40.88, which is optional and conditional on HQLA.",
      "impact": "Position: Prime broker holds 100 of segregated client-protection cash maturing within 30 days, kept in HQLA Reading a: Follow LCR40.44 literally: inflow in 40.87 category (financial institution 100% or 50%) mandatory Reading b: Follow LCR40.88: optional 100% inflow only if balances kept in HQLA Difference: up to 100 of inflow",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
